e:"Conjugated (water-soluble) bilirubin appears in urine (dark) and reduced bile reaches the gut (pale stools), indicating cholestasis/obstruction or hepatocellular disease. Unconjugated hyperbilirubinaemia (haemolysis, Gilbert's) does not cause dark urine."},

